{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1545678-lex-magica-trying-to-understand","id":1545678,"title":"Lex Magica - Trying to understand","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-11-11T01:33:16-08:00","id":1545678,"title":"Lex Magica - Trying to understand","content":"I'm reading now <b>Silver Ladder</b> 1E Order book - and I particularly want to understand Lex Magica. ( For my historical game. ) I understand Gold, Silver, Bronze and Iron Laws. But I still think I don't understand idea of <b><i>Shadows Laws</i></b>.<br /> <br /> From my reading - <i><b>Shadow Laws</b></i> are Tearchs doing 'we make just laws/decisions, even when others don't listen to us'. I.e. Shadow Laws is Tearchs living by virtue of the Law, not the decision of Ruling Council itself. Do I get it right?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 11-11-2024, 01:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-11T02:49:35-08:00","id":1545680,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1545678-lex-magica-trying-to-understand#post1545678\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">From my reading - <i><b>Shadow Laws</b></i> are tearchs doing 'we make just laws/decisions, even when others don't listen to us'. I.e. Shadow Laws is Tearchs living by virtue of the Law, not the decision of Ruling Council itself. Do I get it right?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think so? I'm not entirely clear what you mean by 'living by virtue of the law'.<br /> <br /> The idea is that there is the Lex as it is actually practiced by any given consilium, and there is the Silver Ladder's idealised version of the Lex. The Ladder expects it's membership to abide by this idealised version.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-11T08:29:59-08:00","id":1545696,"title":"","content":"Looking at the description in page 73 of the Order book, my interpretation is that its internal policy. A Shadow Law represents the ideal the Lex should follow according to that Consilium's Silver Ladder chapter.<br /> <br /> Th\u00e9archs are given a command to practice these laws, in this way they become exemplars of their benefits and thus make them more likely to become official Consilium policies.<br /> <br /> A Lictor will take local Shadow Laws into account when judging th\u00e9archs, giving them precedence over local Consilium law, essentially allowing a th\u00e9arch to be tried and punished as part of a Silver Ladder internal affair.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":24280,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","user":"KaiserAfini","date":". 11-11-2024, 11:32 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}